  "description": "Give your next design the charm of a record worth keeping.\nYokai Pop is a vintage Japanese-inspired display typeface that channels the expressive spirit of 1970s vinyl covers. Think carefully composed record sleeves, unexpected color combinations, and lettering that makes you curious about the music before the needle touches the groove. Nostalgic, playful, and full of personality, Yokai Pop brings that same sense of discovery to modern design.\nInspired by an era when album artwork was part of the listening experience, Yokai Pop turns a title into the main attraction. Pair it with warm paper textures and faded tones for a treasured-record feel, or introduce vivid colors and clean layouts to give its vintage character a fresh setting. It invites you to build compositions with rhythm, atmosphere, and a little imagination.\nUse it for album covers, music posters, distinctive logos, boutique packaging, magazine headlines, apparel, café identities, and record-store branding. Whether you’re creating a fictional record label or giving a contemporary brand a nostalgic voice, Yokai Pop helps your typography become part of the story.\nA little vinyl nostalgia. A little Japanese pop. A whole lot of character.",
  "fullDescription": "<p>Give your next design the charm of a record worth keeping.</p>\n<p>Yokai Pop is a vintage Japanese-inspired display typeface that channels the expressive spirit of 1970s vinyl covers. Think carefully composed record sleeves, unexpected color combinations, and lettering that makes you curious about the music before the needle touches the groove. Nostalgic, playful, and full of personality, Yokai Pop brings that same sense of discovery to modern design.</p>\n<p>Inspired by an era when album artwork was part of the listening experience, Yokai Pop turns a title into the main attraction. Pair it with warm paper textures and faded tones for a treasured-record feel, or introduce vivid colors and clean layouts to give its vintage character a fresh setting. It invites you to build compositions with rhythm, atmosphere, and a little imagination.</p>\n<p>Use it for album covers, music posters, distinctive logos, boutique packaging, magazine headlines, apparel, café identities, and record-store branding. Whether you’re creating a fictional record label or giving a contemporary brand a nostalgic voice, Yokai Pop helps your typography become part of the story.</p>\n<p>A little vinyl nostalgia. A little Japanese pop. A whole lot of character.</p>",
